# Task 5 - Restore an EC2 Instance from the Latest Snapshot

## Objective

Automate disaster recovery by restoring an EC2 instance from the latest available EBS snapshot.

## AWS Services Used

- AWS Lambda
- Amazon EC2
- Amazon EBS
- IAM
- Amazon CloudWatch

## Features

- Identifies the latest snapshot for a specified EBS volume.
- Registers a new AMI from the snapshot.
- Waits until the AMI becomes available.
- Launches a new EC2 instance (`t3.micro`) from the AMI.
- Tags the restored instance with the snapshot ID.
- Logs the snapshot ID, AMI ID, and new EC2 instance ID.

